@startuml
title COLORS Web Application - Class Diagram

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
left to right direction

class "JavaScript (code.js)" as JS <<module>> {
  + doLogin()
  + addColor()
  + searchColor()
  + doLogout()
}

class "Login.php" as Login <<API endpoint>>
class "AddColor.php" as AddColor <<API endpoint>>
class "SearchColors.php" as Search <<API endpoint>>

class "Users" as Users <<database table>> {
  + ID : INT (PK)
  + FirstName : VARCHAR(50)
  + LastName : VARCHAR(50)
  + Login : VARCHAR(50)
  + Password : VARCHAR(50)
}

class "Colors" as Colors <<database table>> {
  + ID : INT (PK)
  + Name : VARCHAR(50)
  + UserID : INT
}

JS ..> Login : HTTP POST
JS ..> AddColor : HTTP POST
JS ..> Search : HTTP POST

Login ..> Users : SELECT
AddColor ..> Colors : INSERT
Search ..> Colors : SELECT

Users "1" -- "0..*" Colors : UserID

note bottom of Colors
  UserID links colors to users logically.
  The lab SQL does not explicitly
  declare a foreign key constraint.
end note

@enduml